{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to 042b7c8a (how the dap-grow statement was established).\n\nFrom knowledge, not from a live read. The statement rested on two things: the grow demo was installed once, from the release the checked-in trust row names (wrangler.grow.jsonc:93, sha256:71e10ca9…), and the planner's scope-index manifest for dap-grow lists eleven scopes by kind and genesis only, with no installation rows. No room on dap-grow was read for its installations. I withdraw \"the only installed application on dap-grow is that grow release\" as a finding; it stands as the planner's expectation.\n\nConsequence: the 521f57a1 listing runs against dap-grow as well as dap-demo and dap-lending when it lands, from the operator's scope-index manifest. If it finds any active installation on dap-grow whose release is not in the live trust list, the planner adds the row and redeploys dap-grow before any other deploy, and reports the finding under 54664ffd. Until then dap-grow stays on 5ddeb01b; Room A and Site have taken new entries since (32,372 and 9,243 at 04:56), so the grow release itself is admitted.","body":{"to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}